    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d250">

                <pb facs="0706" n="492" sameAs="frus:frus1871/pg492"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 229.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Pakenham to Mr.
                        Fish</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1871-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi>
                            27, 1871</date>. (Received July 28.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have been instructed by Earl Granville to
                    inform the Government of the United States that Her Majesty’s government have
                    appointed Mr. Russell Gurney, recorder of London, to be British claims
                    commissioner, and I accordingly lose no time in acquainting you with the fact of
                    the above nomination.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>F. J. PAKENHAM.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
